# Rank 1017 / CVE-2026-45300: async-http-client forwards Cookie headers across a
# redirect security boundary. Redirect30xInterceptor.propagatedHeaders strips
# AUTHORIZATION and PROXY_AUTHORIZATION when the redirect crosses origins or
# downgrades HTTPS to HTTP, but leaves COOKIE in place, so session cookies are
# sent to a redirect target the attacker may control (CWE-200, CWE-522). The fix
# 3b0e3e9e removes COOKIE on the same boundary, keeping the NTLM and SCRAM case
# in a separate branch, and relies on the URI-scoped cookie store to re-add
# cookies that legitimately match the new target.
#
# ATTENTION, extractor gap: no method-and-argument pairing for Java. This class
# is generic and recurring rather than one library's mistake, and the correct
# rule is documented: on a cross-origin redirect an HTTP client must drop the
# credential-bearing headers, Authorization, Proxy-Authorization and Cookie
# together. The same omission has produced CVEs in curl, urllib3, requests and
# axios, so a concept for it would not be concept-per-CVE bloat.
#
# The binding cannot be written precisely today. The discriminator is whether
# the function calls remove(COOKIE), and Java's presence-node features expose
# only node.context.callArg, a flat bag of argument texts, with no pairing of a
# call to its argument. Written against that bag the binding is
#   className contains "Redirect" and callArg contains "AUTHORIZATION"
#   and not (callArg contains "COOKIE")
# which separates a reduced vulnerable snippet from its patched form correctly,
# but reports nothing on the real file: matching is case-insensitive and the
# vulnerable function also names Cookie, CookieStore, cookieStore and
# addCookieIfUnset while re-adding cookies from the store, so the negation
# suppresses the true positive. A rule that works on a trimmed snippet and not
# on the code the CVE was filed against is a repro-shaped patch, so the concept,
# rule and bindings drafted here were reverted rather than shipped.
#
# The C frontend already has the feature this needs, node.context.callArgAt,
# holding entries shaped like "callee:index:value" so a binding can require
# "remove:0:AUTHORIZATION" and forbid "remove:0:COOKIE". Probing every form of
# that key against this Java file matches nothing, and the Java frontend never
# populates it. Adding callArgAt to the Java extractor would make this rank
# detectable with a precise, documentation-derivable binding.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1017: redirect header propagation strips Authorization but keeps Cookie"
  lang java
  file client/src/main/java/org/asynchttpclient/netty/handler/intercept/Redirect30xInterceptor.java
  reject VYQL-SEC-008
  code
  ```
  public class Redirect30xInterceptor {
      private static HttpHeaders propagatedHeaders(Request request, Realm realm, boolean keepBody,
                                                   boolean stripAuthorization) {
          HttpHeaders headers = request.getHeaders().copy();
          if (!keepBody) {
              headers.remove(CONTENT_LENGTH);
          }

          if (stripAuthorization || (realm != null && (realm.getScheme() == AuthScheme.NTLM
                  || realm.getScheme() == AuthScheme.SCRAM_SHA_256))) {
              headers.remove(AUTHORIZATION)
                      .remove(PROXY_AUTHORIZATION);
          }

          return headers;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1017: fix also removes Cookie on the security boundary"
  lang java
  file client/src/main/java/org/asynchttpclient/netty/handler/intercept/Redirect30xInterceptor.java
  reject VYQL-SEC-008
  code
  ```
  public class Redirect30xInterceptor {
      private static HttpHeaders propagatedHeaders(Request request, Realm realm, boolean keepBody,
                                                   boolean stripAuthorization) {
          HttpHeaders headers = request.getHeaders().copy();
          if (!keepBody) {
              headers.remove(CONTENT_LENGTH);
          }

          if (stripAuthorization) {
              headers.remove(AUTHORIZATION)
                      .remove(PROXY_AUTHORIZATION)
                      .remove(COOKIE);
          } else if (realm != null && (realm.getScheme() == AuthScheme.NTLM
                  || realm.getScheme() == AuthScheme.SCRAM_SHA_256)) {
              headers.remove(AUTHORIZATION)
                      .remove(PROXY_AUTHORIZATION);
          }

          return headers;
      }
  }
  ```
